<report>
<title>Woolf chi-square analysis of 2 by 2 series</title>
<block name="table">

<p><u>For table @table</u><br />
Percentages:  A = @pc_a C = @pc_c Total = @pc_t</p>
<block name="warn_small"><p><warn>WARNING: SMALL EXPECTED FREQUENCIES, CHECK BY EXACT METHODS</warn></p></block>
<p>Uncorrected Chi&#xb2; = @table_chi_2 Chi = @table_chi<br />
Yates' corrected Chi&#xb2; = @yates_chi_2 Chi = @yates_chi <pval>@{yates_chi_p:pval}</pval></p>

<block name="no_haldane">
<p><b>Without Haldane Correction:</b><br />
Odds ratio = @odds  log odds ratio = @log<br />
Variance of log odds ratio = @var  standard error = @se  weight = @weight<br />
Chi&#xb2; = @chi_2 Chi = @chi<ci> </ci><pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
<ci>Approximate @pc% CI for log odds ratio = @ci_from to @ci_to</ci><br />
<ci>Giving an odds ratio of @odds_from to @odds_to</ci></p></block>
<block name="warn_no_haldane">
<p><warn>ODDS RATIO NOT COMPUTABLE WITHOUT HALDANE CORRECTION</warn></p>
</block>
<block name="haldane">

<p><b>With Haldane Correction:</b><br />
Odds ratio = @odds  log odds ratio = @log<br />
Variance of log odds ratio = @var  standard error = @se  weight = @weight<br />
Chi&#xb2; = @chi_2  Chi = @chi <pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
<ci>Approximate @pc% CI for log odds ratio = @ci_from to @ci_to</ci><br />
<ci>Giving an odds ratio of @odds_from to @odds_to</ci></p>
</block>
</block>
<br />
<block name="combined_no_haldane">
<p><b>For combined tables without Haldane correction:</b><br />
Number of Tables = @tables<br />
Mean log odds ratio = @mean giving odds ratio = @odds<br />
Variance of mean log odds ratio = @var  standard error = @se<br />
<ci>Approximate @pc% CI for mean log odds ratio = @ci_from to @ci_to</ci><br />
<ci>Giving odds ratio of @odds_from to @odds_to</ci><br />
Chi&#xb2; for expected log odds ratio = 0 is @chi_2 Chi = @chi <pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
Chi&#xb2; for heterogeneity = @het_chi_2 DF = @df <pval>@{het_chi_p:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
<block name="combined_with_haldane">

<p><b>For combined tables with Haldane correction:</b><br />
Number of tables = @tablesx<br />
Mean log odds ratio = @meanx giving odds ratio = @oddsx<br />
Variance of mean log odds ratio = @varx  standard error = @sex<br />
<ci>Approximate @pc% CI for mean log odds ratio = @ci_fromx to @ci_tox</ci><br />
<ci>Giving odds ratio of @odds_fromx to @odds_tox</ci><br />
Chi&#xb2; for expected log odds ratio = 0 is @chi_2x Chi = @chix <pval>@{chi_px:pval}</pval><br />
Chi&#xb2; for heterogeneity = @het_chi_2x DF = @dfx <pval>@{het_chi_px:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
</report>
